{
  "$comment": [
    "07 §4.3 rung 2, LOCAL_SEED_TABLE: a hand-curated, in-repo, MIT-licensed table of common",
    "ETFs and funds, keyed by ticker. It exists because rungs 3 and 4 (SEC EDGAR N-PORT, issuer",
    "holdings CSVs) are network calls behind an egress allow-list and rung 5 (name heuristics) is",
    "a guess; the overwhelming majority of a personal portfolio is a handful of broad index funds,",
    "and answering those from a file is both exact and free.",
    "",
    "This is NOT the ~600-row table 07 §4.3 imagines. It is 48 rows, chosen as the funds most",
    "likely to appear in a US personal portfolio, and the honest consequence is stated in",
    "docs/evidence/phase-3/wp3.1-securities.md: the measured hit rate on the seed and the",
    "resulting % unclassified. Growing it is a data edit that needs no code change, which is the",
    "point of it being a file.",
    "",
    "expenseRatio is the issuer's published net ratio as a decimal string (0.000300 = 0.03%), as",
    "of 2026-09. It feeds fee drag only, it is user-correctable through security_overlay, and it",
    "is never a float: NUMERIC(9,6) all the way down (D3).",
    "",
    "components, where present, is the fund-of-funds look-through 07 §4.3 asks for — weights as",
    "decimal strings, recursion capped at depth 3 with cycle detection, and a fund whose weights",
    "miss 1.0 by more than 5% flagged rather than quietly bucketed."
  ],
